Error [E2402]: This implicit fallible call can't convert `<corelib>/Core/auth::Core/auth/auth.jet::AuthError` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> auth_token_keeps_credential_leak_protection.jet:7:15
    |
  7 |     _ := auth.verify_jwt(token, key: key, audience: "gateway")
    |               ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Ordinary fallible calls propagate automatically; `<corelib>/Core/auth::Core/auth/auth.jet::AuthError` can reach `Err` only through `impl <corelib>/Core/auth::Core/auth/auth.jet::AuthError -> Err`
 Fix: Handle this call locally with `??`, add `impl <corelib>/Core/auth::Core/auth/auth.jet::AuthError -> Err { … }`, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402

Error [E0722]: A `Credential` value is denied at `print`
  --> tests/ui/taint/auth_token_keeps_credential_leak_protection.jet:8:5
    |
  8 |     print(token)
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: `print` writes to a log, terminal, or serialized output, where a credential would leak
 Fix: Log a non-secret field, or pass the value through a matching `#Scrub(Credential)` function
